---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { listedPosts, fullTitle, formatDate } from './_posts.js';

// jeyanandan.com -- Jason's personal site, and only that.
//
// 2026-09-24: reordered, at Jason's request. The old page led with Fuckery,
// the most obscure thing here, and that was the wrong first impression. New
// order: who I am, in one line -> what I am working on right now
// (formaddie.com, the most prominent thing on the page) -> the initiatives,
// as a set, in a tile grid, so the whole shape is visible at a glance -> the
// writing, given real prominence instead of a footnote -> the Ko-fi
// disclosure and link. Jason's own lines run through the page between
// sections, as punctuation, spread out rather than clustered. Nothing is
// hidden: Fuckery is still on the page, it is just not the opening line.
//
// 2026-09-28 (night): "minimalistic but subtly epic" (Jason). Same palette,
// same faces, same one accent, still no script. What changed:
//   - The hero is the Being line and nothing else, with room to breathe. The
//     "failing / succeeding" quote that sat directly under it is NOT gone: it
//     moved down, to sit between formaddie.com and Meta DAX, where it belongs
//     (the experiments are the failing). Two quotes in a row was the problem.
//   - Meta DAX has its own feature card, eyebrow "My purpose" (Jason: "it's
//     not my life's work ... it should be my purpose" -- the same word
//     replaced "life's work" in The Fuckarian, where the section is now
//     #my-purpose, and in the Meta DAX post), the same shape as the
//     formaddie.com card: mark, title, date,
//     lede, links, tag. The mark is the DAX Foundation favicon redrawn in this
//     palette as inline SVG (img-src is 'self' data:, and an inline <svg> is
//     the document, not an image request).
//   - Every h2 eyebrow carries a hairline out to the right edge, like a
//     chapter head. Quotes are larger, spaced wider, and carry a short orange
//     tick above them that rhymes with the hero rule.
//   - Motion, all CSS, all behind prefers-reduced-motion in Base.astro: the
//     hero fades up once on load and its rule draws itself; below the fold,
//     sections rise as they enter the viewport, and only in browsers that
//     support scroll-driven animations (@supports gate; everyone else sees a
//     static page, which is the correct fallback).
//   - The closing line is the same line as the hero, and that is now on
//     purpose: it is set as a coda, the largest quote on the page. The page
//     opens and closes on the same sentence.
//
// THE WRITING LIST IS GENERATED. It reads listedPosts (and fullTitle,
// formatDate) from ./_posts.js, the same module /blog/ and /sitemap.xml
// read, so an unlisted post (fuckarian, the-constraint) cannot appear here
// while it is hidden there. fullTitle joins title and subtitle the same way
// the rest of the site does, so a change to that join happens in one place.
//
// MADDIE. The only formaddie.com content on this page is the feature card
// below: the bristlecone mark, one paragraph and the outbound link. The
// demonstration, the recorder, the privacy policy, sign-in and the auth
// callbacks stay off the site; they are kept, unbuilt, in src/_suppressed/
// and the recorder component, unimported, at src/components/Talk.astro. Read
// src/_suppressed/README.md before restoring any of it. The mark is
// self-hosted under /assets/ because the CSP is img-src 'self' data:. Do not
// swap in formaddie-rabbit.svg: its fill is near-white and it disappears on
// this paper background.
//
// TWO DEPLOY GATES. deploy-jeyanandan.yml greps the BUILT page for:
//
//     not the Foundation and not the company.
//     ko-fi.com/jeyanandan
//
// Both sit in the closing Ko-fi paragraph: the disclosure is the sentence
// right after the link (moved there from the hero on 2026-09-28, when the
// hero became the Being line), the second is the link's href. Both must stay real body text (real markup, not a comment)
// on one source line each. Reword either and the workflow has to change in
// the same change-set, workflow first.
//
// 2026-09-28: LinkedIn is the reference for Jason himself. The "failing"
// quote links to his LinkedIn profile (its About section opens with the same
// idea), and the site footer in Base.astro carries a LinkedIn link on every
// page. The closing line is his saying as he says it: "a being that just
// happens to be human".
//
// 2026-09-28 (later): names without the article, as Jason uses them --
// "DAX Foundation" and "Constraint Protocol", not "The ...".
//
// Comments in the markup below are {/* ... */}, never <!-- ... -->. Astro
// emits an HTML comment nested inside an element straight into the built
// page, and a gate sentence living in a shipped comment would pass the grep
// happily while the paragraph it was meant to guard was gone.
---
<Base
  title="Jason Jeyanandan"
  description="I'm a Being that just happens to be human."
>
  <section class="hero"><div class="shell narrow">
    <h1>Jason Jeyanandan</h1>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <p class="lede">I'm a <a class="be" href="https://github.com/ObsidianDelta/Fuckery/blob/main/FUCKERY.md#45-be-be-ing-and-the--ing" title="BE: the ground state (Fuckery v0.51, section 4.5)"><strong>Be</strong></a><a class="ing" href="https://github.com/ObsidianDelta/Fuckery/blob/main/FUCKERY.md#65-consciousness-as-governance" title="The -ing: consciousness, the choosing of your own constraints (Fuckery v0.51, section 6.5)"><em>ing</em></a> that just happens to be human.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="feature"><div class="shell narrow">
    <h2 class="eyebrow">Working on now</h2>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <a class="mark" href="https://formaddie.com"><img src="/assets/formaddie-bristlecone.png" width="140" height="145" alt="formaddie.com" /></a>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3 class="feature-title"><a href="https://formaddie.com">formaddie.com</a></h3>
        <p class="feature-date">Released <time datetime="2026-09-21">21 September 2026</time></p>
        <p class="feature-lede">A senior-facing <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/#cognitive-companion">cognitive companion</a> that turns a life into a memoir by talking. Built at <a href="https://www.obsidiandelta.com">Obsidian Delta</a>.</p>
        <p class="feature-tag">"Your stories will live forever."</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="quote-band"><div class="shell narrow">
    <p class="quote"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jasonjeyanandan" title="Jason Jeyanandan on LinkedIn">"If you're not failing, you're not succeeding."</a></p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="feature"><div class="shell narrow">
    <h2 class="eyebrow">My purpose</h2>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <a class="mark" href="/blog/meta-dax/" aria-label="Meta DAX"><svg class="dax-mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="140" height="140" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect class="dax-tile" width="32" height="32" rx="6"/><circle class="dax-ring" cx="16" cy="16" r="8.5"/><circle class="dax-dot" cx="16" cy="16" r="2"/></svg></a>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3 class="feature-title"><a href="/blog/meta-dax/">Meta DAX</a></h3>
        <p class="feature-date">Public since <time datetime="2026-09-28">28 September 2026</time></p>
        <p class="feature-lede"><a href="https://daxfoundation.org/#learning">DAX Foundation's</a> universal learning initiative: every human being, any subject, free, forever. Now in the open — the first fourteen experiments of countless more to come, and the 2024 prototype that started it.</p>
        <p class="feature-links"><a href="/blog/meta-dax/">The introduction</a><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><a href="https://github.com/daxfoundation/metadax">The repository</a><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><a href="https://youtu.be/pMVwtGqUSh4" title="The 2024 prototype: a fractions course for an eleven-year-old, through baseball (2:27)">The prototype, 2:27</a></p>
        <p class="feature-tag">"Every human being. Any subject. Free, forever."</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="quote-band"><div class="shell narrow">
    <p class="quote"><em>Per aspera ad astra</em> — through hardship, to the stars. The hardship is the route.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section><div class="shell">
    <h2 class="eyebrow">Initiatives</h2>
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile">
        <p class="tile-kind">Foundation</p>
        <h3><a href="https://daxfoundation.org">DAX Foundation</a></h3>
        <p>The mission, and the constraint it answers to — DAX, the preservation and expansion of life, humanity, and consciousness — kept apart from the company that builds the infrastructure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <p class="tile-kind">Company</p>
        <h3><a href="https://www.obsidiandelta.com">Obsidian Delta</a></h3>
        <p>The company. Builds the cognition.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <p class="tile-kind">Public working draft</p>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/daxfoundation/constraint-protocol">Constraint Protocol</a></h3>
        <p>A signed record nobody can quietly edit, and a way for a person, a company or a piece of software to declare in advance what it will not do — and be checked against it. v0.5.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <p class="tile-kind">Metacognitive framework</p>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/ObsidianDelta/Fuckery">Fuckery</a></h3>
        <p>Structure forms under constraint, then becomes the constraint on whatever forms next. Named so that nobody genuflects at it. v0.51, CC BY 4.0.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <p class="tile-kind">Learning initiative</p>
        <h3><a href="/blog/meta-dax/">Meta DAX</a></h3>
        <p>DAX Foundation's universal learning initiative. Every human being, any subject, free, forever. Now public, experiments and all.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="quote-band"><div class="shell narrow">
    <p class="quote">"If you don't fight for your love, what kind of love do you have?"</p>
  </div></section>

  {listedPosts.length > 0 && (
    <section><div class="shell narrow">
      <h2 class="eyebrow">Writing</h2>
      <ul class="posts">
        {listedPosts.map((p) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/blog/${p.slug}/`}>{fullTitle(p)}</a>
            <time datetime={new Date(p.date).toISOString()}>{formatDate(p.date)}</time>
            {p.description && <p>{p.description}</p>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div></section>
  )}

  <section class="quote-band"><div class="shell narrow">
    <p class="quote">"Wealth is not how much money I have. It is how happy and well off the people I love are."</p>
  </div></section>

  <section><div class="shell narrow">
    <p>If any of this is useful to you, <a href="https://ko-fi.com/jeyanandan">buy me a coffee</a>. It goes to me: this is my personal site — not the Foundation and not the company.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="quote-band coda"><div class="shell narrow">
    <p class="quote">"I am a being that just happens to be human."</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>

<style is:global>
/* ---------- the hero: one name, one rule, one line ----------
   A faint warm glow sits above the name, the colour of the accent at a tenth
   of its strength: the only thing on the page that is not paper, ink or the
   accent itself, and it is the accent, diluted. */
.hero{
  position:relative;
  padding:clamp(4.5rem,13vw,9rem) 0 clamp(3rem,8vw,5.5rem);
  background:radial-gradient(60% 55% at 50% -12%,rgba(201,114,36,.11),transparent 70%);
}
.hero h1{
  font-size:clamp(2.6rem,8.5vw,5rem);letter-spacing:-.03em;line-height:1.02;
  margin:0 0 1.25rem;
}
.hero .rule{margin:0 0 1.75rem;transform-origin:left center}
.lede{
  font-size:clamp(1.35rem,3.4vw,2rem);line-height:1.3;letter-spacing:-.01em;
  color:var(--strong);margin:0;text-wrap:balance;
}
.lede a{
  color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;
  text-decoration-color:var(--orange);text-decoration-thickness:1.5px;text-underline-offset:.16em;
}
.lede a:hover{color:var(--orange)}
.lede strong{font-weight:700;color:var(--strong)}
.lede em{font-style:italic}

section + section{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:clamp(2.25rem,6vw,3.5rem) 0}
section p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
section a{text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:.16em}
section a:hover{color:var(--orange)}
section strong{font-weight:600;color:var(--strong)}

/* ---------- eyebrows: a chapter head, the hairline runs to the edge ---------- */
h2.eyebrow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;margin-bottom:1.1rem}
h2.eyebrow::after{content:"";flex:1 1 auto;height:1px;background:var(--line)}

/* ---------- quotes: punctuation between sections, not clustered ----------
   Larger than the body, wider apart, and each one opens with a short orange
   tick that rhymes with the rule under the name. */
.quote-band{padding:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,4.25rem) 0}
.quote-band .narrow{max-width:32rem}
.quote-band .narrow::before{content:"";display:block;width:22px;height:2px;background:var(--orange);margin:0 auto 1.15rem}
.quote{font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-size:clamp(1.2rem,2.8vw,1.5rem);line-height:1.5;color:var(--soft);text-align:center;margin:0;text-wrap:balance}
.quote em{font-style:italic}
.quote a{color:inherit;text-decoration-color:var(--line)}
.quote a:hover{color:var(--orange);text-decoration-color:currentColor}

/* The coda: the page closes on the line it opened with, set largest. */
.coda{padding:clamp(3.5rem,10vw,6.5rem) 0 clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)}
.coda .narrow{max-width:38rem}
.coda .narrow::before{width:56px;margin-bottom:1.5rem}
.coda .quote{font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3.8vw,2.1rem);line-height:1.3;color:var(--strong)}

/* ---------- feature cards: working on now, and my purpose ---------- */
.feature-card{
  display:flex;gap:1.75rem;align-items:flex-start;
  margin-top:.5rem;
  background:var(--card);
  border:1px solid var(--line);
  border-top:3px solid var(--orange);
  border-radius:6px;
  padding:clamp(1.5rem,4vw,2.5rem);
}
.feature-card .mark{flex:0 0 auto;display:block;line-height:0}
.feature-card img{display:block;width:140px;max-width:100%;height:auto}
.feature-body{min-width:0}
.feature-title{font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(1.9rem,4.5vw,2.6rem);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:0 0 .4rem;color:var(--strong)}
.feature-title a{text-decoration:none}
.feature-title a:hover{color:var(--orange)}
.feature-date{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 1.1rem}
.feature-lede{font-size:clamp(17px,2vw,19px);margin:0 0 1rem}
.feature-links{
  display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.6rem .75rem;align-items:baseline;
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 1.1rem;
}
.feature-links a{color:var(--strong);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding-bottom:.1em}
.feature-links a:hover{color:var(--orange);border-bottom-color:var(--orange)}
.feature-links span{color:var(--line)}
.feature-tag{font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--orange);margin:0}

/* The Meta DAX mark: the DAX Foundation favicon, redrawn in this palette.
   Ink tile, bone ring, and the centre dot in the accent. */
.dax-mark{display:block;width:140px;height:140px;max-width:100%}
.dax-tile{fill:var(--ink)}
.dax-ring{fill:none;stroke:var(--bone);stroke-width:2}
.dax-dot{fill:var(--orange);transition:r .25s ease}
.mark:hover .dax-dot{r:3}

@media (max-width:600px){
  .feature-card{flex-direction:column;gap:1.1rem;padding:1.5rem}
  .feature-card img,.dax-mark{width:110px;height:auto}
  .feature-links span{display:none}
}

/* ---------- initiatives: tile grid, the whole shape at a glance ---------- */
.tiles{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr));gap:1.1rem;margin-top:.25rem}
.tile{
  display:flex;flex-direction:column;
  background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;
  padding:1.4rem 1.5rem 1.6rem;
  transition:border-color .2s ease,transform .2s ease;
}
.tile:hover{border-color:var(--orange);transform:translateY(-2px)}
.tile.coming{border-style:dashed}
.tile-kind{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--orange);margin:0 0 .55rem}
.tile h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600;font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 .55rem;color:var(--strong)}
.tile h3 a{text-decoration:none}
.tile h3 a:hover{color:var(--orange)}
.tile p{font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin:0;color:var(--ink)}
.tile .badge{
  align-self:flex-start;margin-top:.9rem;
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--orange);border:1px solid var(--orange);border-radius:3px;padding:.2rem .45rem;
}

/* ---------- writing, given real prominence ---------- */
.posts{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.5rem}
.posts li{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1rem}
.posts li:first-child{border-top:none;padding-top:0}
.posts a{font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600;font-size:1.3rem;line-height:1.3;color:var(--strong);text-decoration:none;display:block}
.posts a:hover{color:var(--orange)}
.posts time{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);margin-top:.4rem}
.posts p{margin:.6rem 0 0;color:var(--muted)}

/* ---------- motion: all CSS, all off under prefers-reduced-motion ----------
   On load the hero fades up in three beats and the rule draws itself. Below
   the fold, each section rises as it enters the viewport (fully in by the time
   its top edge is 180px up, a fixed distance, so a tall section does not sit
   half-faded while it is being read) -- but only where the browser can drive
   an animation from scroll. Anywhere else the @supports
   block is skipped and the page is simply there, which is the right fallback:
   nothing is ever hidden behind a script. */
@keyframes rise{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(14px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}
@keyframes draw{from{transform:scaleX(0)}to{transform:scaleX(1)}}
.hero h1{animation:rise .8s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1) both}
.hero .rule{animation:draw .9s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1) .25s both}
.hero .lede{animation:rise .8s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1) .35s both}
@supports (animation-timeline: view()){
  .hero ~ section{
    animation:rise linear both;
    animation-timeline:view();
    animation-range:entry 0% entry 180px;
  }
}
</style>
